  "stem": "The value of \\(y\\) is inversely proportional to the value of \\(x\\), where \\(x > 0\\). When \\(x = 4\\), \\(y = 9\\). For what value of \\(x\\) is \\(y = x\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "6"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Inverse proportion means \\(xy\\) is constant: \\(xy = 4 \\cdot 9 = 36\\).",
    "If \\(y = x\\), then \\(x^{2} = 36\\), so \\(x = 6\\) (since \\(x > 0\\))."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
